// Illegal: a `Task<T>` field is a refcounted handle, and the struct holding it
// says nothing. The handle in the field has no count of its own, so the release
// the spawning scope emits is the last one and the field is left dangling.
//
// `propagates<pooled>` on the type is what gives the obligation a holder. The
// companion is examples/pass/propagates_full/, which writes the clause.
type Job {
    work: Task<int32>,
}

function main(): int32 {
    return 0;
}
